 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOpenID Connect authorization and token responses broken due to parameter order swap\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using OpenID Connect authorization code flow, the authorization and token endpoints are failing due to incorrect parameter ordering in method calls. The dispatcher methods are passing `token_handler` and `request` parameters in the wrong order to the underlying grant handlers.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.openid.connect.core.endpoints import Server\nfrom oauthlib.openid.connect.core.grant_types import AuthorizationCodeGrant\n\n# Set up a basic OpenID Connect server\nserver = Server()\n\n# Try to create an authorization response\nuri = 'http://example.com/path?client_id=abc&scope=openid&response_type=code'\nheaders, body, status = server.create_authorization_response(uri, scopes='openid')\n\n# This will fail due to parameter order issues in the dispatcher\n```\n\nThe issue also affects token creation:\n\n```python\n# Try to create a token response  \ntoken_uri = 'http://example.com/path'\nbody = 'client_id=me&redirect_uri=http://back.to/me&grant_type=authorization_code&code=test_code'\nheaders, body, status = server.create_token_response(token_uri, body=body)\n\n# This will also fail due to parameter swapping\n```\n\nAdditionally, when using hybrid flow with nonce values, the nonce parameter is being incorrectly set to None instead of using the actual nonce from the request.\n\nThe authorization code dispatcher is also returning None for empty requests instead of properly handling them, and the token dispatcher is incorrectly using `token_handler` instead of `request` when determining the handler.\n</issue>\n",
